<title>UK: UK machine tool turnover up 13.5% latest quarter.</title>
<headline>UK machine tool turnover up 13.5% latest quarter.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Turnover of machine tools in Britain rose a seasonally adjusted 13.5 percent in the three months to January over the previous three months, the Office for National Statistics said on Thursday.</p>
<p>This was due to a 23.7 percent jump in export turnover and an eight percent rise in home turnover. Compared with the same period a year ago, total turnover increased by 4.1 percent.</p>
<p>Total orders on hand for machine tools at the end of January were 2.1 percent lower than at the end of October 1996, but 10.2 percent up on January 1996.</p>
<p>-- Mike Peacock, London Newsroom +44 171 542 5109</p>
